(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Care transitions for advanced cancer patients often lack coordination across institutional) Tj
T*
(boundaries, compromising quality and continuity. The Pal-Cycles intervention targets these) Tj
T*
(gaps through structured communication and care planning protocols. Given substantial) Tj
T*
(variation in European healthcare systems and end-of-life practices, successful) Tj
T*
(implementation requires systematic adaptation to local contexts. This protocol describes) Tj
T*
(the adaptation methodology for Pal-Cycles across seven countries spanning different) Tj
T*
(healthcare funding models, regulatory environments, and cultural frameworks. Adaptation) Tj
T*
(employs structured nominal group techniques with iterative refinement through) Tj
T*
(multistakeholder consultation. Clinician working groups in each country will collaborate) Tj
T*
(with patient/family advisory panels \(where feasible\) to refine intervention components) Tj
T*
(while maintaining theoretical fidelity. Subsequent implementation uses a stepped-wedge) Tj
T*
(design to evaluate outcomes including implementation reach, fidelity measures, and) Tj
T*
(preliminary clinical and process endpoints. This paper details the systematic approach to) Tj
T*
(cross-cultural adaptation of complex palliative care interventions.) Tj
